DTSTART:20261031T174500Z
DTEND:20261031T194500Z
SUMMARY:A Talent for Murder
LOCATION:Triplex Cinema\, 70 Railroad St\, Great Barrington\, MA 01230
DESCRIPTION:Times: 1:45pm\, 7:30pm\nA young man travels from New York to Sw
 itzerland to try to persuade acclaimed thriller writer Patricia Highsmith 
 to write one final installment of her Tom Ripley series\, with his efforts
  gradually turning more sinister.\nhttps://www.thetriplex.org/movie/a-tale
 nt-for-murder\nFrom Pushpin Western Mass: https://pushpin.city/westernma/
URL:https://www.thetriplex.org/movie/a-talent-for-murder
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:6a5792273936aa36ab6c36cf8aa088b8a403f7b6@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20261031T193113Z
DTSTART:20261031T180000Z
DTEND:20261031T200000Z
SUMMARY:The History of Concrete
LOCATION:Triplex Cinema\, 70 Railroad St\, Great Barrington\, MA 01230
DESCRIPTION:Times: 2pm\, 5pm\nFollowing the finale of his acclaimed HBO ser
 ies How To with John Wilson\, NYC-based documentarian John Wilson looks to
  the bedrock of his beloved New York City for inspiration and structure. C
 oncrete\, the world's most widely used building material\, appears as an e
 ver-present life force\, and John sets out to make the definitive document
 ary on the matter. To tell this seemingly drab story\, he decides to use t
 he industry-approved Hallmark formula to increase his movie's appeal. But 
 his foundation soon begins to crumble—literally and figuratively—as he
  struggles to balance artistic freedom with the realities of the modern fi
 lm industry.\nhttps://www.thetriplex.org/movie/the-history-of-concrete\nFr
 om Pushpin Western Mass: https://pushpin.city/westernma/
URL:https://www.thetriplex.org/movie/the-history-of-concrete
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aadf8ee20a60602f96f90fe5b9b157233dcc01ab@pushpin.city
DTSTAMP:20261031T193113Z
DTSTART:20261031T181500Z
DTEND:20261031T201500Z
SUMMARY:The Only Living Pickpocket in New York
LOCATION:Triplex Cinema\, 70 Railroad St\, Great Barrington\, MA 01230
DESCRIPTION:Times: 2:15pm\, 5:15pm\, 8:15pm\nHarry Lehman is an aging pickp
 ocket who plies his trade with ever-diminishing returns in a drastically c
 hanged New York. Wallets stuffed with cash have been replaced by easily ca
 ncelled credit cards\, and Harry struggles to make ends meet as he cares f
 or his disabled wife\, Rosie. When he unwittingly purloins and fences a va
 luable USB stick\, Harry finds himself in a race against time to return th
 e loot or face the rage of a vengeful crime family.\nhttps://www.thetriple
 x.org/movie/the-only-living-pickpocket-in-new-york\nFrom Pushpin Western M
 ass: https://pushpin.city/westernma/
URL:https://www.thetriplex.org/movie/the-only-living-pickpocket-in-new-york
END:VEVENT
